 ## How the kanji combine
 
-[片](../kanji/片.md) contributes a part or fragment; [仮名](仮名.md) (かな) is kana, a writing-system term. Within that term, 仮 relates to provisional or borrowed use and [名](../kanji/名.md) to naming; learn the contracted 仮名 reading かな as a unit rather than inventing freely reusable individual readings. Many katakana shapes developed from parts of kanji, but that is not an exceptionless account of every shape.
